caption: Seedlings

Chaos sometimes designates people as Seedlings. Seedlings are not Champions and receive none of the special Champion privileges unless separately granted. A Seedling receives one Class for free. Chaos determines how the Class is selected; normally the Seedling chooses it, but Chaos may choose, restrict the available Classes, or use some other procedure. The campaign determines whether this grant can ignore the Seedling’s Species Class List.

Seedlings use the Drive system for advancement. Being a Seedling does not itself grant any particular Drives; they use whatever Drives the campaign provides. This is true even in campaigns where ordinary adventurers would use regular adventure or session experience instead.

Seedlings also receive some form of protection from permanent death, determined by the campaign. The protection may change substantially from one game to another. Seedling status itself does not define the exact return, respawn, reincarnation, or other survival procedure.
